# REGWATCH QA gold set -- the retrieval release gate.
#
# One JSON object per line; "#" lines are comments and are skipped by the loader.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVERY expected_sources entry carries a verbatim "quote" from that exact
# (short_name, page). regwatch.eval.verify_gold asserts the quote really appears
# there and that every expected_fact is present in some cited source, and
# run_eval REFUSES to score a gold set that fails verification -- before it
# spends a single LLM call.
#
# This is not ceremony. An audit on 2026-08-05 found 3 of the original 12 rows
# carried wrong page attributions (25%). A wrong page does not fail loudly; it
# quietly depresses recall and citation precision for a CORRECT answer, which
# pressures the team into lowering the CI thresholds to fit the broken asset --
# after which the gate is calibrated to its own errors, a real regression fits
# inside the slack, and a real IMPROVEMENT reads as a regression.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Every row carries a "category" from regwatch.eval.metrics.GOLD_CATEGORIES so
# the scorecard can say WHICH kind of question a change broke, not merely that
# something did. Categories are stratified, NOT sampled in proportion to real
# query volume: the failures that matter most in a regulatory answer (a dropped
# exception clause, a cross-document contamination) are rare in traffic and
# severe in consequence.
#
# CORPUS CONSTRAINT: the CI gate seeds only psg_crawler.SEED_APPL_NOS (8
# documents, ~66 chunks). A question pinned to any other document is
# unanswerable in CI and fails the gate on every run.
#
# ALBUTEROL TRAP: albuterol sulfate has TWO dosage forms in the corpus
# (PSG_020503 Aerosol, Metered / Inhalation and PSG_017853 Tablet / Oral). Any
# albuterol question that is NOT a clarification row MUST name its dosage form,
# or the multi-form guard fires and the row scores as a clarify, not an answer.
#
# CURRENT_VERSION -- 14 rows. Ordinary answerable retrieval against the current
# version of a document; covers all 8 seeded PSGs.
